s the $x$-axis and $b=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124652 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89fbf42b-d171-5772-87ce-cf622b720963" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces and Cylinders With Alternative Orientations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b797dee-ca3e-5c3b-85ce-6b2632a48d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281939} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5637fb-da12-5dea-a981-e26928513ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282481} {:answer/id #uuid "5f796707-fea7-5500-bb97-01eb443bbac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282495} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8bbf9c-44e3-598b-935c-30694436809c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282740} {:answer/id #uuid "a64d6ece-5046-54c2-9ee2-1ed2c37bc66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A couple of planes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f796707-fea7-5500-bb97-01eb443bbac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282495} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e64324-99b5-5e27-9546-09c8e362586a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44fe2c9a-8d31-5524-87d8-4678d7fc0908" :question/math-academy-id "q-164546" :question/problem "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=8x,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis and $p=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124652 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89fbf42b-d171-5772-87ce-cf622b720963" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces and Cylinders With Alternative Orientations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232f26c9-79a9-5402-b0f7-63e58ec7851c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282000} {:answer/id #uuid "7c568ec1-5072-5178-846a-7f2b606d9954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A couple of planes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282761} {:answer/id #uuid "9283fa33-e3d9-51e6-a60b-d84331b8323d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282952} {:answer/id #uuid "ce57cf6e-a823-5536-bf65-94a57901af34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283492} {:answer/id #uuid "eefd41c3-ba1b-5b3d-8bc1-3c2122e2528a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "232f26c9-79a9-5402-b0f7-63e58ec7851c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282000} :answer-field/id #uuid "05d7e5ed-5266-504a-b7eb-960c915d96ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe349944-268d-5340-92ca-d28764061da5" :question/math-academy-id "q-164548" :question/problem "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=-12y,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis and $p=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124597 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "549870ce-a18a-5a94-a9ea-f3de72aaac1f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10cde161-28f6-55e5-986b-ad9855da614a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(-1,2,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281844} {:answer/id #uuid "122b7f1a-d06c-5752-b881-d3aaf0a1f656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,-2,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281863} {:answer/id #uuid "49873a52-1e06-5d10-9048-c31a56b3f6fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282313} {:answer/id #uuid "ca420948-0b66-53de-bd82-72e7dc4965ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283457} {:answer/id #uuid "d9275452-1c1f-54aa-9f44-b0b79feef1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca420948-0b66-53de-bd82-72e7dc4965ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283457} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd434c9b-d384-57dd-8332-85e7b5ec2000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b66372b-0da7-5bff-8ad5-ecdf16f5fac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-164549" :question/problem "Identify the surface ${y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-4y)-({z}^{2}+6z)-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4-(z+3)^{2}+9-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2} & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124597 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "549870ce-a18a-5a94-a9ea-f3de72aaac1f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adad1d8-ee29-5dc9-a2ee-653fa19ae072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(0,-1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281789} {:answer/id #uuid "0b5de068-06c5-56af-ba40-a7a1e7dfa46c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A ellipsoid centered at $(0,-1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281794} {:answer/id #uuid "60439c74-0d03-59a4-b541-10d37912b306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(0,-1,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282504} {:answer/id #uuid "a738f849-3d2b-54c1-bbe9-c98b25d774ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283144} {:answer/id #uuid "ee439119-77c9-5b1e-9934-a94b64201e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee439119-77c9-5b1e-9934-a94b64201e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283767} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec4e70e8-a589-565e-9fac-45096d9a65cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2297e678-9e2f-50f7-bf32-a9e17f605ed6" :question/math-academy-id "q-164550" :question/problem "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+2y)+2({z}^{2}-4z)-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2[(z-2)^{2}-4]-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2(z-2)^{2}-8-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124597 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "549870ce-a18a-5a94-a9ea-f3de72aaac1f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1243d3b-361e-5bdf-975f-049a3ec6fa01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401546} {:answer/id #uuid "fa487f89-3be7-5d40-961d-7546309e11de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401547} {:answer/id #uuid "025044f2-a8e8-56c9-abcc-e56e1609a263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheet centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401548} {:answer/id #uuid "1c63b753-83a9-5faf-9522-2b10200701ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401549} {:answer/id #uuid "a76c934a-6a50-5b6b-97fe-08774387e03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa487f89-3be7-5d40-961d-7546309e11de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401547} :answer-field/id #uuid "fffbfe5a-e6b2-509f-a19b-67c3c7c49922" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "040e9acf-1af9-5813-86f6-e469cb0eecc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-164553" :question/problem "Identify the surface $5{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}+20x+10z+15=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}+20x+10z+15 & =0 \\\\ 5({x}^{2}+4x)-{y}^{2}-5({z}^{2}-2z)+15 & =0 \\\\ 5[(x+2)^{2}-4]-{y}^{2}-5[(z-1)^{2}-1]+15 & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-20-{y}^{2}-5(z-1)^{2}+5+15 & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-{y}^{2}-5(z-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ -5(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+5(z-1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124597 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "549870ce-a18a-5a94-a9ea-f3de72aaac1f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa81a3d-635f-57e1-9a94-bf37f98dfd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,2,-2).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281973} {:answer/id #uuid "2e173800-0b97-51fd-afb1-068806054b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282092} {:answer/id #uuid "64aae431-c6e3-5110-b292-f1311622a080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282552} {:answer/id #uuid "a78cb202-bdaf-5810-a67e-f452bfe11a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(-1,-2,2).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283145} {:answer/id #uuid "c435a85b-2eaa-5f57-9889-bdeb2d10e25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(-1,-2,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64aae431-c6e3-5110-b292-f1311622a080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282552} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc88e78b-63ab-59c2-8f80-b4d0d1a43dd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acd3345e-478a-507e-b6c0-b18910d49c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-164554" :question/problem "Identify the surface $2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12 & =0 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x)-4({z}^{2}+4z)-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x-1)^{2}-1]-4[(z+2)^{2}-4]-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-2-4(z+2)^{2}+16-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2} & =y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124597 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "549870ce-a18a-5a94-a9ea-f3de72aaac1f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2cc085-a59d-56dd-81bb-d07371a2a8a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,0,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321763} {:answer/id #uuid "9f341fa3-f683-52a6-b968-2e33e82139a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322401} {:answer/id #uuid "a2aefb17-f02a-54e5-8595-b45603b4b42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322431} {:answer/id #uuid "e4541fbb-55e3-509e-9780-1f3f16ce74e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322935} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ba0df8-5f49-5933-bd23-7a1a9d327e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(2,0,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f341fa3-f683-52a6-b968-2e33e82139a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322401} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aeb3d56-ad05-5134-a623-f1ab028e5a1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8b7d35e-9f56-5494-bc85-89ac721410ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-36110" :question/problem "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+4x)+{y}^{2}-25({z}^{2}-2z)+91 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x+2)^{2}-4]+{y}^{2}-25[(z-1)^{2}-1]+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-16+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+25+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1).$"}]}
